=============================================================
BUSINESS RULES TO IMPLEMENT
=============================================================

BR-001: Web Crawl Scheduling
- Schedule crawls per source URL independently
- Compare current crawl vs previous snapshot
- Only forward new/updated listings downstream
- Log failures, flag timed-out sources
- Config-only source management (no runtime modification)

BR-002: Rule Engine Filtering
- Apply filters in sequence: keyword → industry → geography 
  → contract value → deadline → eligibility pre-conditions
- ALL mandatory filters must pass for a listing to proceed
- Log the exact filter that caused each rejection
- Use only approved/versioned filter rules

BR-003: Document Acquisition & Ingestion
- Download attached documents per passing RFP listing
- Support PDF, Word, HTML, plain text
- If no attachment, process from listing page directly
- Preserve structure: headings, tables, numbered lists, appendices
- Flag corrupted/unreadable sections → route to HIL
- Link document to unique RFP identifier

BR-004: Task Decomposition & Skill Mapping
- LLM analyzes scope of work → decomposes into tasks
- Each task gets priority level + RFP section reference
- Identify required skills, experience levels, domain expertise
- Classify skills as mandatory or preferred
- Output structured JSON → submit for Manager review

BR-005: Certification Identification
- Extract all certification requirements from RFP
- Classify as mandatory or preferred
- Link to task + RFP section + page reference
- Validate against certification taxonomy
- Flag unrecognised certifications for HIL

BR-006: Risk & Eligibility Analysis
- Compare RFP requirements vs capability register + past performance
- Assign eligibility status: Eligible / Conditionally Eligible / 
  Not Eligible
- For Conditionally Eligible: identify gaps + mitigation actions
- Identify delivery risks with initial severity ratings
- Submit outputs for Manager review before go/no-go decision

BR-007: Structured Output Packaging
- Aggregate all outputs into single versioned JSON object
- Include: crawl source, filter record, tasks, skills, 
  certifications, eligibility, risks, confidence scores
- Block downstream handoff until HIL confirmation recorded

BR-008: HIL Review & Correction Logging
- Route output to HIL queue after generation
- Require Manager action: confirm / correct / reject
- Block all downstream processing without confirmation
- Log every correction: rfp_id, field_name, original_value, 
  corrected_value, reviewer_id, timestamp
- Queue correction data for prompt/rule improvement cycles

