=============================================================
CONFIDENCE SCORING RULES
=============================================================
- Every extracted field MUST carry a confidence score (0.0 to 1.0)
- Threshold: 0.7
- Score < 0.7 → flag for HIL review, withhold from confirmed output
- Score >= 0.7 → auto-approved
- Risk bands: 0.0-0.5 (low), 0.5-0.7 (medium), 0.7-1.0 (high)

=============================================================
LLM PIPELINE LOGIC
=============================================================
Build a LangChain pipeline with the following stages:

Stage 1 — Document Chunking
- Split large RFP documents into chunks respecting section boundaries
- Maintain section metadata per chunk

Stage 2 — Task Decomposition Chain
- System prompt: Extract all tasks and deliverables from RFP scope
- Output: structured JSON with task name, description, priority, 
  effort, section reference
- Include confidence score per task

Stage 3 — Skill & Certification Extraction Chain
- System prompt: Identify all skill and certification requirements
- Classify as mandatory or preferred
- Tag with source section and page reference
- Validate certifications against taxonomy list
- Include confidence score per field

Stage 4 — Eligibility Assessment Chain
- System prompt: Compare RFP requirements against capability profile
- Output eligibility status with supporting evidence
- Identify gaps and suggest mitigations
- Include confidence score

Stage 5 — Risk Assessment Chain
- System prompt: Identify key delivery risks from RFP
- Assign severity ratings
- Include confidence score per risk

All prompts must be:
- Version-controlled via PromptTemplate model
- Only approved versions used in production
- Plain-English rationale included in every output

=============================================================
CELERY PIPELINE TASKS
=============================================================
Build the following Celery tasks chained in sequence:

1. task_crawl_source(source_url_id)
2. task_apply_rule_engine(rfp_listing_id)
3. task_download_document(rfp_listing_id)
4. task_parse_document(rfp_document_id)
5. task_decompose_tasks(rfp_id)
6. task_extract_skills_certifications(rfp_id)
7. task_assess_eligibility(rfp_id)
8. task_assess_risks(rfp_id)
9. task_package_output(rfp_id)
10. task_notify_hil_reviewer(rfp_id)

Each task must:
- Write to AuditLog on start and completion
- Handle failures gracefully with retry logic
- Never proceed to next stage without previous stage success
- Block at task_notify_hil_reviewer until HIL confirmation recorded

=============================================================
NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
=============================================================
- Processing time per RFP: < 30 seconds under normal conditions
- Concurrent RFP processing: minimum 50 in parallel
- Crawl success rate: >= 80% with max 3 retries, 30s timeout
- Scalability: up to 1000 RFPs/day
- Uptime: 99.5% target
- Encryption: TLS 1.2+ in transit, encrypted at rest
- Audit log retention: 7 years
- All timestamps in UTC
- All outputs in English regardless of source language

